  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Backend**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the full-stack design for this Nostalgia Video Generator. Right now, I\'m focusing on making the backend fully compliant. It\'ll be called `server.ts`. I\'m figuring out the communication flow with Gemini; specifically, I need to check how to access the API key via `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`.\n\n\n**Initializing the Gemini SDK**\n\nI\'m now initializing the Gemini SDK using the provided configuration, including the API key from environment variables. I\'ve also decided on \'gemini-3.5-flash\' as the model for these text-based tasks, considering its speed and quality. Next, I\'m designing the schema for the prompt\'s output to include scene numbers, titles, and image/video prompts, all matching the user\'s formulas.\n\n\n**Formulating the Video Prompt**\n\nI\'m currently crafting the video prompt using a first-person perspective, framing the shot as if the viewer *is* the character. I\'m focusing on the hands interacting with specific, nostalgic objects and describing the room\'s lighting and background items, all customized to match the user\'s specific decade and region requirements. The goal is to capture a vivid, lived-in feel. I\'m also ensuring the prompt captures a 35mm film aesthetic, with grain and an amateur quality.\n\n\n**Refining the Scene Details**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the nuanced details within each scene. The focus is on incorporating subtle, micro-movements, like a thumb on a D-pad or a finger tracing a cassette tape. I\'m also describing lighting shifts, and ensuring the motion feels grounded and natural, not overly dramatic. I\'m aiming for an immersive feeling that perfectly captures the character\'s nostalgic absorption.\n\\n\\n\nOkay, I\'m setting up a `responseSchema` for the model to ensure structured JSON outputs. This prevents any parser issues. I want the backend to return clean and elegant data. I will structure the data with an array of scenes, each with appropriate properties.\n\n\n**Defining the Schema**\n\nI\'ve crafted a comprehensive `responseSchema` to guarantee structured JSON outputs from the model. This is key to preventing parser issues and ensuring the backend returns clean, elegantly structured data. The schema features an array of scenes, each with detailed properties. Each will contain the scene\'s number, title, `targetDevice`, and other necessary data.\n\n\n**Structuring the Prompt**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring the AI adheres perfectly to user templates for image and video prompts. I\'m building this structure into the system prompt itself, so that it can substitute the culturally accurate details. To do this, I will need to make some progress on designing the user-friendly interface.\nI\'ve outlined an application interface design that includes interactive decade and theme selection through preset buttons, search options, and audience settings, providing customization for all kinds of nuances. I\'m now crafting the prompt generator sandbox for visual results, making sure everything is aligned.\n\n\n**Designing the Frontend**\n\nNow, I\'m delving into the frontend design, envisioning an interactive editing board with a retro aesthetic. Each scene will be displayed with its number, title, and a placeholder image or an animated visual. I\'m exploring the feasibility of incorporating a \"Generate Preview Image\" function using the Gemini API, recognizing the need to navigate potential paid key requirements and user capabilities.\n\n\n**Adding Image Generation**\n\nI\'ve just realized a \"Generate Preview Image\" function for each scene would be amazing. I\'m exploring the `gemini-2.5-flash-image` model, as detailed in `gemini-api/SKILL.md`. I\'ll create a backend endpoint for image generation, adding interactivity. I\'ve confirmed that the standard API key will work server-side.\n\n\n**Designing the UI**\n\nI\'m now detailing the UI elements for each generated scene, planning copy buttons for image/video prompts and a combined promo script. I\'m also planning a \"Nostalgia Mood Board\" detail card, showing parsed variables from the prompt, alongside aesthetic text-reveal animations. Plus, I want to create a \"POV Scene Director\" mode with settings for real-time prompt adjustments. Finally, I\'m working on a saved concepts drawer that uses `localStorage`.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will modify the scripts in `package.json` to enable a robust full-stack development experience (using `tsx server.ts` as our dev compiler and compiling our backend server via `esbuild` for production deployment). This allows us to securely execute the Gemini API on the backend."
