    thinking: "**Constructing Server Logic**\n\nI\'m now focused on building the `server.ts` backend. My primary task is to initialize `@google/genai` using the API key from the environment. I\'ll need to set up the connection to Vite middleware for development environments and expose the necessary API endpoints.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'ve specified the `/api/generate` endpoint, designed to take either a decade or custom theme input, along with an optional demographic. I\'m crafting a JSON response schema to ensure a strongly-typed array of scenes from Gemini 3.5. My focus is now on the system instructions, ensuring the AI acts as an expert \"Nostalgia Video Generator,\" delivering 5 detailed scenes in a strict format, including title, target device or object, lighting source, and background items.\n\n\n**Refining Scene Generation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the fine-grained scene specifications. Each scene will be structured with micro-movements, lighting changes, and a precisely formatted image prompt. The image prompt will be in the first-person POV, capturing the viewer\'s experience, with forearms and wrists interacting with the \"targetDevice,\" dimly lit by the \"lightingSource,\" against the \"backgroundItems.\" The scene has a raw, authentic feel.\n\n\n\n**Expanding API Features**\n\nI\'m now thinking about adding an `/api/image-preview` endpoint. It would use `gemini-2.5-flash-image` to generate a preview of the scene. I can use the same text prompt format as the existing endpoint. The focus is on integrating this image preview with the existing scene generation workflow. I\'ll need to figure out how to best integrate this for the user, and what the optimal response schema looks like.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create the backend entry point `/server.ts` which handles express routing, parses requests, calls the server-side Gemini API with structured JSON output, optionally offers image preview generation using the modern `@google/genai` client, and mounts Vite in development/production modes."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 404258456
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
